### Deedify API Test Requests
### Use this file in VS Code with REST Client extension or JetBrains HTTP Client

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@userId = test-user-123
@listingId = test-listing-456
@orderId = test-order-789

### 1. Create a PENDING order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "listingId": "{{listingId}}",
  "quantity": 10,
  "amount": 10000
}

### 2. Process fiat payment webhook (simulates success)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/fiat/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "{{orderId}}",
  "status": "success",
  "txHash": "mock_tx_hash_123"
}

### 3. Get all orders for a user
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/user/{{userId}}

### 4. Get specific order by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}

### 5. Get API documentation
GET {{baseUrl}}/api

### 6. Health check (if implemented)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Example with real data (replace with actual IDs from your database)
### Create order with real user and listing IDs
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "clx1234567890abcdef",
  "listingId": "clx0987654321fedcba",
  "quantity": 25,
  "amount": 25000
}

### Process webhook with real order ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/fiat/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "clx1111111111111111",
  "status": "success"
}